WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
<b>Ryoin</b>

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
<b>Jinko</b>

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.150
The first half's almost over.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.380
Pile-up!

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.130
The first half is over!

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.900
12-0, Jinko's leading!

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.510
All right!

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.500
First- and second-years.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:33.000
<b>Episode 25
All Out</b>

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:33.000
Sorry we third-years kept making 
mistakes during the first half.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.750
It's totally fine.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.220
That try was super cool.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.680
It was sheer luck.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.260
Anyway, try to last the whole game.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:41.400
Roger!

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.260
<i>So they're aware of their own performance.</i>

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.890
<i>In that case, there's nothing 
for me to say to them.</i>

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.700
What's gotten into you guys?

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.780
I hardly recognize you out there.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:03.030
You're all fearlessly putting 
yourselves out there.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.780
You're still not as fast as they are,

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.930
but you are reacting to them.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:11.040
You're looking good.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.330
But don't let it get to your heads.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:17.210
They'll come at us during the second half.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.990
Don't forget the focus
you had in the first half.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:21.700
That's all.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.070
Fight with everything you've got!

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.570
Yes, sir!

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:32.040
You know what I'm going to say, don't you?

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:35.060
Your passes are faster.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:39.150
Your skills and technique 
are way better, too.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:42.590
So why did you let them score two tries?

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:45.560
Presumption.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.120
We completely underestimated them.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:53.180
Because we assumed such a weak team 
didn't stand a chance against us,

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.330
they scored two tries.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:00.470
That's right. I don't have any advice for you.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.190
Just take them seriously.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.400
That's all.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.570
By the way, regardless of the outcome,

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:12.200
the second string and Tsukinaka
will be punished with extra practice.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:12.770
What?

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:13.540
Yes, sir!

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.020
<b>Crushed</b>

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.020
Why?

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.270
The second half will now begin.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.370
Jinko!

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.570
Go!

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.110
All right!

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:30.690
I was surprised you agreed 
to play Jinko, Coach.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.870
Is there something you wanted 
to achieve through this game?

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.450
Of course.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:41.010
The second string's shortcomings 
are already being exposed.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:44.570
When you win too much, you become arrogant.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:47.390
I'm no exception.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.270
Honestly, I'm surprised by Jinko's play.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:57.800
I didn't know their coach used to
play for the national team, either.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.050
He seems pretty good.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:01.780
Apparently, he keeps a blog.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:03.270
I saw it.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:07.280
He says he's been putting them
through meaningless, prehistoric drills.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.530
It's almost heartwarming.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:15.540
And it's probably true. 
They're not doing anything special.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:21.040
What's special is how much 
his players want to win.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:28.090
They don't think this is just a practice game.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:34.120
And they're not letting us walk over them
just because we're champions.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.600
At this rate, they'll develop 
even more confidence.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:42.610
With the Kanagawa preliminaries coming up,
nothing could be worse for us.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:48.570
A player's mental state
has a powerful effect on the game.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.590
What should we do about it?

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:01.020
Jinko!

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:09.680
Sekizan!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.180
Damn it.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:15.680
Jinko's failure to release the ball!

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.490
All right! Got 'em back!

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.500
Sekizan, don't worry about it.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:28.420
It's Ryoin's line-out.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:31.160
Jinko, don't let them through!

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:34.410
<i>They're leaving a pretty large gap.</i>

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:36.230
<i>Which way will they go?</i>

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.170
Behind!

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:50.010
I'm through!

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:00.110
Try!

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:03.270
Nice try, Mikado!

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:05.770
No big deal!

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.280
Focus on the next play.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:12.020
Ryoin made the kick.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:13.950
It's 12-7 now.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.100
Don't worry about it, Jinko!

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.450
You're winning!

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.300
What do you want?

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:38.650
You'll have to join them for 
extra practice, after the game.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:50.230
Ref, Ryoin would like to 
make a player substitution.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:55.710
At number eight, Tosa is being 
subbed out for Zanba Ryujin.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.100
Are you sure, coach?

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:03.730
Yeah, but we can't reveal our cards.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:05.080
We'll have him play number eight.

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:08.220
We probably could've won 
without subbing him in,

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:14.090
but I want to destroy Jinko's confidence.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.320
Y-You can't be serious.

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:19.600
I thought we were playing 
their second string.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:22.640
It's the giant of Ryoin.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.560
You're up, tree trunk.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:27.360
What? What are you talking about?

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.110
Why is Zanba taking the field?

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:37.700
We can't let Jinko's morale get any higher.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:43.260
We need to whip the demotivated 
second string into shape, too.

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:45.960
I wouldn't worry about that.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:50.960
Ryujin's a genius at breaking a team's
momentum and changing the mood of a game.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:57.220
<i>We can't let Ryoin get the ball.</i>

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:00.220
<i>I have to get the ball here
and keep the attack going.</i>

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:11.000
Iwashimizu!

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.220
Zanba's coming!

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:14.510
Stop him!

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.740
You shithead!

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:31.110
Piece of shit!

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:33.300
I'll kill you!

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:40.800
Nice.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.030
Try!

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:03.290
It's nice how you guys go all out.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:08.790
I think it's really important 
to want to kill your opponent.

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:12.040
I feel the same way.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.790
I want to kill you, too.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.590
Fun, right?

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.340
Don't miss, Kaiji.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:30.930
Wh-What was that? 
It must be against the rules.

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:33.860
They game's momentum changed in an instant.

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:42.100
K-Komori-san.

00:10:44.780 --> 00:10:47.620
Why do you look so disheartened?

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:51.380
What happened to the expressions 
you were wearing until now?

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.390
That's a pass from a national team player.

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.770
Looks like you can catch it.

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:09.520
You've still got fight in you.

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:11.180
Fight.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.470
Give everything you've got 
until the very last second!

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:16.970
Yes, sir!

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:35.170
I don't like how he plays.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:41.010
These past two years, I've worked 
harder than anyone else on the team.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:44.500
Even though I'm short. 
Even though I puked blood.

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:50.000
But his play makes all 
that effort for naught.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:54.560
He destroys both his opponents'
and his teammates' motivation.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:02.070
What's wrong, Sekito? 
Should I have subbed you in instead?

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.340
My hard work's worth more than that.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:10.500
It's not over yet.

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:13.080
We can still get it back!

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:30.640
We're running out of time.

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:38.900
It's the final play!

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:04.090
<b>Ryoin</b>

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:04.090
<b>Jinko</b>

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:04.090
<b>First Half</b>

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:04.090
<b>Second Half</b>

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:04.090
<b>Total</b>

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.720
The game's over.

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:07.710
Thank you, Minamoto-san.

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:10.470
That was very informative.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:14.350
No, thank you.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:13.830
Come on, it's time for our punishment.

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:14.350
Yes, sir.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.970
Hey, you'll pay for this!

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:18.420
Next time, we won't lose!

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:19.460
Shut up, midget!

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:21.980
We'd never lose to weaklings like you!

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.730
Sekizan, are you okay?

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:25.660
Yeah.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:26.990
Hey.

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:31.820
That was fun.

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:34.740
You know...

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:38.400
I like you guys.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:42.380
You played all out the whole time.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:45.270
Th-Thank you.

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:51.280
I don't think a good rugby player
is someone who's fast,

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:56.130
or someone who's skilled, 
or someone who's big and strong.

00:13:56.990 --> 00:14:02.070
It's someone who excites the people 
watching him with his play.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:08.030
Someone who makes you unable to 
sit still after watching him.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:10.920
Someone whose passion is infectious.

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:14.070
I'm not sure how to explain it,

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:19.150
but I had fun because you guys had that.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.270
Let's face off again.

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:25.050
In an official game next time.

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:30.220
Ryujin, hurry up.

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:32.010
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:32.570
Huh?

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:34.840
Hey, put me down!

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:38.230
Ryujin! Let go! Hey!

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.300
Stay still.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.040
Shudder

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:45.030
<b>It's time
for extra
practice!!!</b>

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:45.030
<b>Tsukinaka,
hold the
tackle bag!!</b>

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:45.030
<b>Why me?!!</b>

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:45.030
<b>Ultimately the captain was the most beat up after the game</b>

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:45.030
<b>Fine, bring
all of them
on, dammit!!</b>

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:49.240
The game just ended. Where are we going?

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:53.440
The upperclassmen said 
we're going to Davos Hill.

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:56.740
Davos Hill? What's that?

00:14:56.740 --> 00:15:01.250
I don't know, except that we're going there.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:05.220
This is Davos?

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.230
It's so open.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:10.340
There's so much greenery. 
Negative ions everywhere.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.550
The first-years are having a good time.

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:17.350
There aren't any negative ions here.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.630
We didn't put much effort
into our hike last year, but...

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:23.860
Yeah, this year...

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:28.020
You worked hard these past five days.

00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:31.120
There was a lot for us to learn, too.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:34.120
We'll continue this conversation at the top.

00:15:35.090 --> 00:15:38.370
Sprint to the peak!

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:41.120
What?!

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:42.140
<b>DOOM</b>

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.380
I knew it.

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:45.070
How far is it to the top?

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:46.420
I don't know!

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:47.880
Come on, let's go!

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:49.970
Gramps, can you hike up there?

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:54.190
I don't know. I'll stop if I can't.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:57.420
The captain will handle
the conversation at the top.

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:58.410
What?

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:01.640
Gion, speak respectfully to your superiors!

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:09.030
This is pretty steep.

00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:12.280
I hate Davos.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.070
There's too much grass, and it's muddy.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:18.040
Did you come here with 
your rugby school, too?

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:23.040
Everyone makes you run here, 
when you come to Sugadaira.

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:25.590
This is tough.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:33.770
Hirota-senpai, you can do it!

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:40.180
Is that Ebumi-senpai in the front?

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:41.670
He's so far ahead.

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:44.370
This place messes with your depth perception.

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:48.440
Damn it! Ebumi's not going to beat me!

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.900
Gion-kun, watch out.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:56.740
This brings back memories.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:58.790
When we were first-years,

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:02.800
it rained in the morning, so it 
was even muddier than it is now.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:06.330
Yeah, and Hirota-kun actually 
rolled down the hill.

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:08.750
I remember that.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.670
Hey!

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:13.360
Did you just talk shit about me?!

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:14.810
His hearing's so good.

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:17.500
We weren't talking shit!

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:20.650
Man, this sucks.

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:24.930
This is the last time
we'll run up this hill together.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:38.510
Hirota tripped again!

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:41.460
Hirota, stop rolling.

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:44.550
Shut up! Don't look!

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.410
Coach.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:49.160
We caught up.

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:53.520
W-Wait...

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:53.520
Pull yourself together.

00:17:53.520 --> 00:17:54.880
Well, well, Yoshida-sensei.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:57.710
I'm envious that you've got a 
pretty young lady on each arm.

00:17:57.710 --> 00:18:00.180
What? Coach, please.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:02.300
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:07.410
Thank you for taking our things to the inn.

00:18:07.970 --> 00:18:10.700
Ikuta-san, thank you for helping, too.

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:12.780
I-It's fine.

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:18.780
My uncle was complaining the whole time, 
but today's game got him really excited.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:23.620
He asked you to beat Ryoin 
and come again next year.

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:27.250
We have Komori-san to thank for that.

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:31.530
No, it's because of those boys.

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:34.290
I didn't fight.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:41.760
They're the ones who fought 
on the field and excited us.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:47.400
They're the true flowers who moved us today.

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:50.420
They deserve your praise.

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:55.590
I'm just a pile of moldy leaves.

00:18:57.040 --> 00:19:01.280
Come on, Coach. What does that make me?

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:05.860
Huh? Water or a worm, I guess.

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:09.820
What? I don't want to be a worm.
I'd rather be a pansy.

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:12.310
Were you listening?

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:16.460
And you're earth, Yoshida-sensei.

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:23.970
They're finally here.

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:28.810
K-Komori-san, are you okay?

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:33.520
Damn. I used to be able to run laps
up and down this hill.

00:19:34.290 --> 00:19:37.070
Yossen's in even worse shape!

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:40.780
Yoshida-sensei, you look 
like a ratty old cloth!

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.740
I haven't seen this view in a while.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:50.290
What do you think of
the peak of Davos, first-years?

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.170
It feels awesome.

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:07.230
I forgot what I wanted to say.

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:12.010
Whatever. Meeting's over.

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:13.190
What?

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:16.700
Captain, say something to the team.

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:18.940
Huh? Uh, yes, sir.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.450
We finally won.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:35.950
Then we faced our opponents with 
everything we had, but still lost.

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:38.100
That was frustrating.

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:43.970
But I have a feeling we learned a lot.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:49.660
These five days, I've worked harder
than I ever have in all my life.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:56.600
You're talking about yourself?

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:59.500
What? Oh, no, uh...

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.110
I feel the same way.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.140
Me, too.

00:21:03.140 --> 00:21:04.360
Me, too.

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:07.000
Us, too. Right, Kashi?

